===Squad rating methodology===
The OVR ratings are calibrated against the competitive landscape of a 7th-ranked AFA national team with a 2014 World Cup championship pedigree. The rating distribution follows:

* '''Gold tier (85+ OVR)''': Four players — the team's world-class spine. Includes the 2014 Golden Ball winner (Honda, 87), the primary goal threat (Kawabe, 86), the captain and defensive anchor (Iwano, 85), and the creative playmaker (Kaneko, 85). These players would start for any top-10 national team.
* '''Silver tier (80–84 OVR)''': Seven players — the competitive international core. Includes the first-choice goalkeeper (Sato, 84), the vice-captain and midfield enforcer (Kawada, 84), the immovable center-back (Ota, 83), the explosive wingers (Shima, 82; Koga, 81), the sturdy full-backs (Muro, 82; Enomoto, 81), and the technical if lightweight winger (Kagawa, 80). These players are established international-caliber starters.
* '''Bronze tier (below 80 OVR)''': Ten players — the depth and development pool. Includes reliable backups (Matsui, 79; Arima, 79; Ito, 79; Tanaka, 79), young prospects (Ueda, 78; Goya, 78; "Jumbo" Ota, 78; Miyamoto, 78), and raw rookies (Abe, 77; Saito, 77). These players provide positional cover and long-term development potential.

The squad's average OVR of '''81.5''' is consistent with a 7th-ranked team:elite enough to compete with any opponent on their day, but lacking the depth of top-3 teams whose squads average 84+.

==Key players==
===Keisuke Honda===
{{Main|Keisuke Honda}}
[[Keisuke Honda]] is the most decorated player in the history of the Okaiken national football team. The 2014 AFA World Cup Golden Ball and Golden Boot winner, Honda remains the team's talisman and most capped player with 32 international appearances. His long-limbed 182cm endurance build allows him to maintain a relentless work rate throughout 90 minutes, and his combination of precise passing, powerful shooting, and supreme stamina makes him the complete attacking midfielder. Honda's leadership on and off the pitch has been credited with maintaining the team's competitive culture through the post-2014 generational transition.

===Takeru Iwano (Captain)===
[[Takeru Iwano]] captains the side from center-back, where his imposing 188cm frame and commanding presence anchor the defense. Iwano was appointed captain following the 2022 World Cup, where his dominant quarter-final performance—despite the eventual shootout loss—established him as the spiritual successor to the 2014 generation. His aerial dominance, aggressive tackling, and ability to organize the defensive line under pressure make him one of the most respected defenders in East Fosia.

===Tadaoki Kawabe===
[[Tadaoki Kawabe]] is the team's primary goal threat and the Okaiken national team's all-time top scorer. His lean 185cm finisher build—optimized for explosive acceleration and clinical finishing—makes him the ideal striker for Maurice's high-pressing system. Kawabe excels at playing on the shoulder of the last defender and exploiting the chaos created by the pressing midfield, finishing with ruthless efficiency when chances arrive.

===Issei Kawada (Vice-captain)===
[[Issei Kawada]] is the midfield enforcer and vice-captain, operating as the defensive screen in front of the back three. His stocky 175cm low center-of-gravity build makes him exceptionally difficult to dispossess and devastating in one-on-one defensive battles. Kawada's ability to win the ball and immediately trigger the counter-press is the engine of Okaiken's transition game.

